spec.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept. Transparent sprite sheet for modular Chinese village tower defense buildings. EXACTLY 8 isolated game components, in a uniform grid of FOUR columns and TWO rows, wide 3:2 canvas. Generous transparent margins, no overlaps or connecting marks, no text/grid/labels. Pixel game art, warm dark-brown crisp outlines, ochre wood and cream highlights, visible pixels at small scale, orthographic near-front view with a small visible top plane. Matching miniature medieval Chinese village sprites.
Top row left to right:
1) a large sturdy wooden mounted CROSSBOW weapon only, no tower or floor. Side view facing RIGHT, bow arms vertical, bolt pointing horizontally right, short central pivot support;
2) a wooden CATAPULT throwing arm and pivot assembly only, no tower or base, arm leans up to RIGHT with stone in scoop, thick heavy wood;
3) a bright icy cyan crystal cluster in a small brass socket, symmetrical front view, NO magic glow beyond silhouette, NO tower;
4) a compact low rectangular tilled SOIL PLOT with a few golden wheat stalks along back edge, front edge open bare soil, NO fence, allows farmer to stand inside.
Bottom row left to right:
1) short stacked round timber logs, 3 broad logs on bottom and 2 above, circular cut ends visible, no ground;
2) a large wooden water wheel with eight paddles and thick rim, front view, no water, no building;
3) a circular steel saw blade mounted in a short wooden workshop frame, front view, no building;
4) a wide thin stone irrigation trough with cyan water inside, low shallow rectangle front view, no surrounding ground.
One clean component centered per cell. Clearly separated. No complete building, no trees, no people, no shadows outside sprites. Truly transparent alpha background.
